## Summary
The article examines a scenario where a CEO's salary appears to be reduced by 93%, attributing this to enhanced executive compensation disclosure rules that may create a misleading optical illusion. It discusses the implications for corporate financial reporting and transparency.

## Key Points
- CEO salary shows an apparent 93% cut in disclosed figures.
- Stricter disclosure regulations for executive pay are implemented.
- This may result in an optical illusion distorting compensation perceptions.
- The case highlights challenges in accurately interpreting financial data.
- It underscores the need for clarity in corporate compensation reporting.


